From d8e96376cc146b4d6bd8080377cff3a9d7fb9433 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:25:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 56/60] v8: template keyword for the dependent Tuple<> calls in
 the Int64 lowering

Int64LoweringReducer<Next>::LowerClz and LowerCtz spell

    __ Tuple<Word32, Word32>(result, __ Word32Constant(0))

i.e. Asm().Tuple<...>(...) on the dependent Asm().  GCC 16 resolves
the template-id Tuple<Word32, Word32> to the class template
turboshaft::Tuple that unqualified lookup finds in the enclosing
namespace: "invalid use of 'struct Tuple<WordWithBits<32>,
WordWithBits<32>>'" (-Wtemplate-body) and then "instantiating
erroneous template" from int64-lowering-phase.cc.  Clang, the only
compiler upstream runs on 32-bit targets, binds the name to the
assembler's member template instead.  The reducer is instantiated
only under V8_TARGET_ARCH_32_BIT (int64-lowering-phase.cc), so the
64-bit GCC builds upstream does see never parse these lines.

Write `__ template Tuple<Word32, Word32>(...)`, which both compilers
accept: the spelling this file already uses for
`__ template Projection<0>(input)` in Unpack(), and the one upstream
main has since adopted for the same two lines (as
`__ template MakeTuple<Word32, Word32>(...)` after the member's
rename).  ScopedVar<Word32> converts to V<Word32> (assembler.h
operator V<U>), so the explicit arguments stay as they are.

Sweep: explicit-template-argument calls through `__` without
`template` in the turboshaft sources are these two plus 19 in
graph-builder.cc and turbolev-graph-builder.cc, where Asm() is a
concrete type and the member lookup is not dependent; the other
32-bit-only turboshaft regions (growable-stacks-reducer.h,
machine-optimization-reducer.h, the `if constexpr (Is64())` else
branches) contain no such call.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 v8/src/compiler/turboshaft/int64-lowering-reducer.h | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/v8/src/compiler/turboshaft/int64-lowering-reducer.h b/v8/src/compiler/turboshaft/int64-lowering-reducer.h
index ee6fe95..6cb8c25 100644
--- a/v8/src/compiler/turboshaft/int64-lowering-reducer.h
+++ b/v8/src/compiler/turboshaft/int64-lowering-reducer.h
@@ -637,7 +637,7 @@ class Int64LoweringReducer : public Next {
       result = __ Word32CountLeadingZeros(high);
     }
 
-    return __ Tuple<Word32, Word32>(result, __ Word32Constant(0));
+    return __ template Tuple<Word32, Word32>(result, __ Word32Constant(0));
   }
 
   V<Word32Pair> LowerCtz(V<Word32Pair> input) {
@@ -650,7 +650,7 @@ class Int64LoweringReducer : public Next {
       result = __ Word32CountTrailingZeros(low);
     }
 
-    return __ Tuple<Word32, Word32>(result, __ Word32Constant(0));
+    return __ template Tuple<Word32, Word32>(result, __ Word32Constant(0));
   }
 
   V<Word32Pair> LowerPopCount(V<Word32Pair> input) {
